      "correctAnswer": [
        "A",
        "B",
        "C"
      ],
      "solution": {
        "finalAnswer": "Statements 1, 2 and 3 are correct.",
        "stepByStep": [
          "Swapping the order flips the direction: $\\vec{a}\\times\\vec{b} = -(\\vec{b}\\times\\vec{a})$.",
          "$|\\vec{a}\\times\\vec{b}|$ is the parallelogram area.",
          "Parallel vectors give $\\sin\\theta = 0$, so the product is the zero vector.",
          "The result is a VECTOR, not a scalar, so the last statement is false."
        ],
        "formulaUsed": [
          "|a x b| = |a||b| sin(theta)"
        ],
        "commonMistake": "Treating the cross product like the dot product (which gives a scalar).",
        "examinerNote": "Direction follows the right-hand rule."
